ly it is as the fbi says  probably  the greatest criminal sting operation in  living memory but there are those issues  of privacy that defendants are likely  to be going into now the fbi  had indicated that it had taken legal  uh precautions every single step of the  way and this is why it started in  australia it would appear  to allow the fbi to be able to get its  legal ducks in a row so to speak  to be able to get the search warrants  all the necessary legal requirements  to do what is essentially hidden  surveillance  of individuals and organizations that  the fbi  had completely entrapped in terms of  what they were doing so there will be  discussion no doubt it will come before  the courts when the  uh defendants appear before the courts  we do know as well  that a grand jury has been empaneled  within the united states 18 individuals  will appeal before that grand jury now  in those discussions which are of course  secret  there's likely to be a lot of debate  about privacy concerns  despite the fbi's uh saying that this is  a  major major achievement thank you so  much mikana reporting from washington  d.c
 

